# Wave W17-S (Route 128): sunk sand — deep-channel sand: a cool, darker shore sand lying in deep water on the Perennial approach, its flecks sparse — the channel is deep here and the bottom shows only in flecks through the swell (design: the last run south over a trench with something breathing under it; the lane\u2019s sand is a rumour of shore). Route 128\u2019s own sand — the fleet\u2019s sparsest sand, and its coolest: split from Route 127\u2019s warm kelp-shadowed sand by temperature and cover, and from Route 129\u2019s pale lee sand by depth. Spec presence is thin by nature (2 cells ship) — the plan\u2019s pre-recorded R40-class exception.
